# Recursive Relational Observation: Native Leaf Boundary Acquisition IV

This continuation studies acquired control, persistent designated-sensor
ambiguity and paid late recovery on the native leaf-boundary source.
Sections 103–110 continue the numbering of
[Native Leaf Boundary Acquisition III](RECURSIVE_RELATIONAL_OBSERVATION_NATIVE_LEAF_BOUNDARY_ACQUISITION_III.md)
(NLBAIII); its Definitions 75.1, 87.1 and 89.1 specify the unchanged source
and fresh growth. NLBA and NLBAII denote the
[first](RECURSIVE_RELATIONAL_OBSERVATION_NATIVE_LEAF_BOUNDARY_ACQUISITION.md)
and [second](RECURSIVE_RELATIONAL_OBSERVATION_NATIVE_LEAF_BOUNDARY_ACQUISITION_II.md)
volumes; references to §§49, 60–65 and 77–86 belong to NLBAII.
AA denotes [Atomic Generation Acquisition](RECURSIVE_RELATIONAL_OBSERVATION_ATOMIC_GENERATION_ACQUISITION.md),
and AGAIII its [third volume](RECURSIVE_RELATIONAL_OBSERVATION_ATOMIC_GENERATION_ACQUISITION_III.md).
These are ordinary conditional proofs, without a new Lean verification.

